<title>SINGAPORE: Serial System debuts to high of S$0.615.</title>
<headline>Serial System debuts to high of S$0.615.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electronic parts distributor Serial System made its debut on Wednesday to hit a high of Singapore S$0.615 against its initial offer price (IPO) of S$0.58.  </p>
<p>At 0109 GMT, the stock has changing hands at S$0.60 after touching a low of S$0.595. Volume was 1.28 million units.</p>
<p>The company had offered 37 million shares in its IPO comprising 27.75 million public shares at S$0.58 each and 9.25 million placement shares at S$0.60 each.</p>
<p>The public portion of the offer was 14 times subscribed.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
